(7580607, 1217480, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>So yeah, who could resist the puppy dog eyes beaming in to their pet owner?:-) Here it is not about food but ''can we come in...where it is nice and warm and plenty of nice cozy warm seats?" This just radiates cuteness. Instead of a straight on shot this one is angled and I feel it actively places the viewer in the frame as one approaches the door this is what we see. Great job in capturing the right moment where you have the Yorkie on the far left looking in, the Yorkie in the middle paws up on the sill beaming cute rays, and the one on the far right is also captured in frame in the window pane.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. So yeah, who could resist the puppy dog eyes beaming in to their pet owner?:-) Here it is not about food but ''can we come in...where it is nice and warm and plenty of nice cozy warm seats?" This just radiates cuteness. Instead of a straight on shot this one is angled and I feel it actively places the viewer in the frame as one approaches the door this is what we see. Great job in capturing the right moment where you have the Yorkie on the far left looking in, the Yorkie in the middle paws up on the sill beaming cute rays, and the one on the far right is also captured in frame in the window pane.', '2018-07-10 23:27:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7580626, 1217729, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I really like the title! It plays well into the presenting this as a group of musicians on stage as well as a nod to the Nesting Dolls with each having an instrument painted on the wooden bodies. I also love how you arranged the dolls in this composition - a ''triangle'' line up with one of the smaller dolls taking center stage as the main lead. Speaking of stage, the black backdrop does allow the dolls colors and detailed paint work to really shine but it is a touch to stark. And if you were going for the imagery of these dolls being a band on stage then it needs that extra something to solidly cement that idea. It shouldn''t be too busy because you don''t want to detract attention away from the dolls with any patterns or a backdrop that is too busy. The only thing I can really think of at this time is maybe some parted red curtains on either side - like the curtains were just opened to reveal the Matroyshka band on stage. Just a thought.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I really like the title! It plays well into the presenting this as a group of musicians on stage as well as a nod to the Nesting Dolls with each having an instrument painted on the wooden bodies. I also love how you arranged the dolls in this composition - a ''triangle'' line up with one of the smaller dolls taking center stage as the main lead. Speaking of stage, the black backdrop does allow the dolls colors and detailed paint work to really shine but it is a touch to stark. And if you were going for the imagery of these dolls being a band on stage then it needs that extra something to solidly cement that idea. It shouldn''t be too busy because you don''t want to detract attention away from the dolls with any patterns or a backdrop that is too busy. The only thing I can really think of at this time is maybe some parted red curtains on either side - like the curtains were just opened to reveal the Matroyshka band on stage. Just a thought.', '2018-07-10 23:42:03.000000', NULL, 1),
